// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// A column definition ends with `(PRIMARY_KEY | NOT_NULL)?` -- an ALTERNATION, not a set.
// A column may be declared a primary key, or not null, but never both in one declaration.
//
// This is where SQL intuition actively misleads: `ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL` is
// ordinary DDL, and a rewrite that models the tail as a loop of optional column flags --
// the natural design, since more flags could be added -- accepts it. legend-engine does
// not. Dropping `NOT NULL` makes this parse.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::PkAndNotNull
(
   Table T
   (
      ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
      VAL VARCHAR(32)
   )
)
